{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Meromorphic.NormalForm","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.Constructions"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio.hr_ratio_phiBProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio.hr_ratio_phiBProd","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdHrRatio.lean#L82-L96","doc":"**`hr_ratio` for `phiBProd`.** For a normal-form strip-growth second solution `Φ₁`: where\n`phiBProd b z ≠ 0`, the meromorphic normal form of `Φ₁/phiBProd` agrees with the pointwise\nratio. This discharges the `hr_ratio` input of the G5 specialization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio.analyticAt_of_stripGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio.analyticAt_of_stripGrowth","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdHrRatio.lean#L60-L80","doc":"**A strip-growth second solution is analytic where `phiBProd` is nonzero** (given it is in\nnormal form). Comparability bounds `‖Φ₁‖` by `C‖phiBProd‖`; `phiBProd` is continuous and\nnonzero at `z`, so `Φ₁` is bounded on a punctured neighborhood, giving order ≥ 0, i.e.\nanalytic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio.phiBProd_analyticAt_of_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio.phiBProd_analyticAt_of_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdHrRatio.lean#L42-L58","doc":"**`phiBProd` is analytic where it is nonzero.** `phiBProd = num/den` with `num`, `den`\nentire; `phiBProd z ≠ 0` forces `den z ≠ 0`, so the quotient is analytic at `z`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}